#import "release.typ": release, release-box, plain-words, signing
#show: release.with(
  title: "Kiki's Cat Club Adoption Agreement",
  intro: [*Thank you for giving a rescued cat a home!* This is the agreement between Sun Brewed Homestead Inc. ("the Homestead"), through its Kiki's Cat Club rescue program, and you, the adopter, for the cat described below. Please read all of it, especially the boxed release, and ask us about anything unclear before you sign. Below, "I" means you.],
  note: [Signed electronically. The signer must be 18 or older.],
  details: ("Cat's name and description", "Microchip number", "Adoption fee (USD)"),
)

#plain-words[
- The cat becomes yours. Keep it indoors, see a vet within 14 days, and never declaw it.
- If you ever can't keep the cat, bring it back to us, never to a shelter.
- Rescued cats' histories are often unknown. *Once the cat is yours, you agree not to sue us over anything it does, even if we were careless.*
]

*1. Transfer.* On signing and payment of the adoption fee, ownership of the cat passes to me. The fee helps cover the cat's care and is not refundable. Because I receive a cat for it, the fee is not a tax-deductible donation.

*2. Health and history.* The Homestead has told me what it knows about the cat's health, age, temperament and history, and has given me its medical records. The cat has been spayed or neutered, or will be before or as California law requires. I understand that a rescued animal's full history is often unknown and that *the Homestead makes no guarantee or warranty about the cat's health, temperament or behavior.* I will take the cat to a veterinarian within 14 days of adoption.

*3. Care.* I will provide the cat with proper food, fresh water, shelter, a clean litter box, companionship, and veterinary care, including yearly check-ups, vaccinations and prompt treatment of illness or injury. I will keep the cat indoors or in a secure enclosure, and will not let it roam. I will not declaw the cat (declawing is banned in Los Angeles and California) and will not use it for breeding, research, fighting or as a gift for someone else.

*4. Identification and local law.* I will update the microchip registration to my name and contact details within 30 days, keep it current, and comply with local animal laws, including the City of Los Angeles's spay/neuter and microchip requirements if I live there.

*5. If I can't keep the cat.* I will not sell, give away, abandon or surrender the cat to a shelter. I will contact the Homestead first and, if it asks, return the cat to Kiki's Cat Club. No fee will be refunded.

*6. Follow-up.* The Homestead may contact me after the adoption to see how the cat is doing. If I gave false information to adopt, or the cat is neglected or mistreated, I will return it to the Homestead when asked.

#release-box(warning: [It gives up your right to sue us over the cat, including for our own carelessness.])[7. Release of liability and assumption of risk][
*I understand that cats can scratch, bite, cause allergies, carry illness that can pass to people and other animals, and damage property, and I assume these risks. I accept responsibility for the cat from the time I take it home. To the fullest extent the law allows, I, for myself and my household, release, and agree not to sue, the Homestead and its directors, officers, volunteers, members and agents for any injury, illness, death or damage to people, animals or property caused by the cat after adoption, INCLUDING CLAIMS ARISING FROM THEIR ORDINARY NEGLIGENCE* (for example in assessing the cat's history or health). This does not release gross negligence, willful misconduct, or any claim the law does not allow to be released. I will indemnify them against claims brought by others for harm the cat causes after adoption.
]

#signing[*8. General.* This agreement is governed by California law. If any part is held unenforceable, the rest remains in effect. I agree to sign electronically, and my electronic signature and initials bind me as if written by hand. *I am at least 18. I have read this agreement and had the chance to ask questions about it, I understand I am giving up substantial rights, including the right to sue, and I sign it voluntarily.*]
